;. /source_outline_flow
  ;= Maintain a source outline
    Bind a captured Markdown file through the existing filesystem source hand. This procedure validates its retained native identity, decomposes headings and blocks, and prepares a Nenex tree. The same filesystem foot owns watching; missing files leave the source input unavailable while previous attempts and documents remain retained.
    ;@ /flow/definition source_outline
    ;= Source outline procedure
      ;@ /flow/input sources
      ;= Current source evidence
        Attach an existing filesystem capture using watch_sources with source, mount, name manual, and format md. Bind this input to the resulting source cell. No generated JSON envelope is needed.
      ;@ /flow/invoke checked ;/0x11/app/nenex/w/evidence_sources_flow/flows/evidence_sources
      ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
      ;= Invoke shared evidence validation
        Create and publish the Evidence sources example first. This caller captures the same reusable child procedure as the handbook.
      ;@ /flow/step structure ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/decompose
      ;@ /flow/bind sources checked
      ;= Decompose Markdown into inert Semidoc nodes
        Source prose cannot author executable flow bindings. Repeated headings receive separate document addresses.
      ;@ /flow/step pages ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/documents
      ;@ /flow/bind pages document
      ;@ /flow/bind sources structure
      ;= Compose the document tree
      ;@ /flow/result pages
      ;= Result
      ;@ /flow/page /
      ;@ /flow/uses manual
      ;= Source outline
        The reference children expose the current source's sections. Review the proposed documents and publish through the existing guarded writer, or attach maintenance through the normal flow hand. Unavailable evidence must be restored before publication can proceed.
